 share of the general seats. That is why these members' names are never on the ballot."},{"questionBn":"Can a woman stand for a general seat as well?","answerBn":"Yes. The reserved seats are an extra opportunity, not a limit. In this Parliament, 7 women have won general seats by direct vote."},{"questionBn":"Are the duties of a member for a reserved seat different?","answerBn":"No. Voting in Parliament, bringing bills, asking questions, sitting on committees: all of it is the same as for members for general seats. The only differences are the way they are elected and that they have no constituency of their own."}],"sourceBn":"The Constitution of the People's Republic of Bangladesh, Article 65; members' names and parties from the Parliament of Bangladesh."}